Conceptually, combine:
1. 	Predictive model of your hand (from step 5)
2. 	Reaction model of the bug (step 1–2)
3. 	Optionally, a generative component (e.g., a tiny transformer) that proposes creative escape maneuvers.
A simple learned‑pattern agent (no transformer yet):

///////////////////////////////////////////////
def smart_bug_step(bx, by, recent_hand_positions,
                   bridge_y, bridge_h, speed=3, Rh=150, Rv=200):
    # 1. Predict where the hand will be
    hx_pred, hy_pred = predict_next_hand(recent_hand_positions)

    # 2. React to predicted hand, not just current
    bx_new, by_new = bug_step(bx, by, hx_pred, hy_pred,
                              bridge_y, bridge_h, speed, Rh, Rv)
    return bx_new, by_new
